Package: gsp670
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3-hidapi
Recommends: pipewire,
            wireplumber
Suggests: python3-dbus,
          python3-gi
Description: Linux support for the EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 headset and GSA 70
 This package provides Linux support for the EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 wireless
 gaming headset and the GSA 70 wireless dongle.
 .
 It installs the udev rules that grant hidraw access to the device, a systemd
 unit that recovers the ALSA card when the kernel binds the audio interfaces
 without registering one, and a WirePlumber configuration that keeps the
 USB-audio nodes from being torn down while idle.
 .
 The optional Python library adds device controls: sidetone, noise reduction
 and auto-power-off, plus device identity and event monitoring.
 .
 Note that the GSA 70 dongle firmware has a bug that adds roughly 1.4 seconds
 of audio latency. Wired USB-C mode has about 44 ms latency. See the README
 for details.

Package: gsp670-dbus
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         gsp670 (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3-dbus,
         python3-gi
Description: D-Bus service for the EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 headset
 Exposes the GSP 670 device controls (sidetone, noise reduction, auto
 power off) and link/battery state on the system D-Bus, so that desktop
 environments and control panels can reach them.
